          "parts": [
            "Here is the **best, safest order** to use a **TENS unit, red light therapy, heat, and ice**, based on how each affects inflammation, blood flow, and nerves.\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 **Recommended Order (Most Cases)**\n\n### **1\ufe0f\u20e3 Red Light Therapy**\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"red light therapy device near back pain\",\"red light therapy muscle recovery\"]}\ue201\n**Why first:**  \n- Increases cellular repair and circulation  \n- Reduces inflammation at a mitochondrial level  \n- Prepares tissue for everything that follows  \n\n**Time:** 10 to 20 minutes  \n**Skin:** Clean, dry skin\n\n---\n\n### **2\ufe0f\u20e3 TENS Unit**\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"TENS unit back pain placement\",\"TENS unit electrode placement lower back\"]}\ue201\n**Why next:**  \n- Blocks pain signals to the brain  \n- Relaxes muscle guarding  \n- Works better once tissue is warmed and oxygenated  \n\n**Time:** 15 to 30 minutes  \n**Tip:** Comfortable intensity, not painful\n\n---\n\n### **3\ufe0f\u20e3 Heat OR Ice (Choose One, Not Both Back-to-Back)**\n\n#### \ud83d\udd25 **Use Heat If:**\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"heating pad lower back pain\",\"heat therapy muscle relaxation\"]}\ue201\n- Muscles feel tight, stiff, or spasmed  \n- Pain is chronic or lingering  \n- No visible swelling  \n\n**Time:** 15 to 20 minutes  \n\n---\n\n#### \u2744\ufe0f **Use Ice If:**\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"ice pack lower back pain\",\"cold therapy inflammation relief\"]}\ue201\n- There is inflammation, swelling, or nerve irritation  \n- Pain feels sharp, burning, or acute  \n\n**Time:** 10 to 15 minutes  \n**Always wrap ice**, never directly on skin\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udeab **Important Rules**\n- Do **not** ice immediately after heat (wait several hours)  \n- Do **not** use heat on active inflammation  \n- Do **not** use TENS over broken skin or directly over spine hardware  \n- If you recently had an injection or flare, **ice is usually better than heat**\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 **Quick Cheat Sheet**\n**Healing focus:**  \nRed light \u2192 TENS \u2192 Heat  \n\n**Inflammation or nerve flare:**  \nRed light \u2192 TENS \u2192 Ice  \n\n---\n\nIf you want, tell me:\n- Where your pain is (neck, low back, hip, nerve path)  \n- Whether this is post-injection, chronic, or a flare  \n- What time of day you are using it  \n\nI can fine-tune this into a **morning vs evening protocol** for you."
          ]
